[{"source": "architecture", "severity": "warning", "category": "memory-safety", "title": "test_role_absent_demand_inert double-frees the trimmed entries array (defer + catalogs_destroy)", "location": "core/demand_test.odin:529-535", "evidence": "\ttrimmed := make([dynamic]Demand_Entry, 0, 4, context.allocator)\n\tdefer delete(trimmed)\n\tfor e in e3.entries {\n\t\tif e.source_role == .Small_Biz || e.source_role == .Campus {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tappend(&trimmed, e)\n\t}\n\tdelete(e3.entries)\n\te3.entries = trimmed\n--- and core/catalog.odin:981-982 (runs later via defer catalogs_destroy(cat2)):\n\tfor i in 0..<len(cat.demand.eras) {\n\t\tdelete(cat.demand.eras[i].entries)", "detail": "Ownership of `trimmed` is transferred to cat2.demand.eras[2].entries, but the LIFO `defer delete(trimmed)` frees the same buffer before catalogs_destroy(cat2) frees it again. Reproduced: `odin test core` emits `+++ bad free @ ... [catalog.odin:982:catalogs_destroy()]`; removing only that defer removes the report.", "recommended_fix": "Delete the `defer delete(trimmed)` line — ownership passes to cat2 and catalogs_destroy already frees eras[2].entries."}, {"source": "architecture", "severity": "note", "category": "coverage-gap", "title": "W9 crowd assertion is tautological after the seeded re-pin but its message still says \"growth must place\"", "location": "core/demand_test.odin:615-619,726", "evidence": "\thost_pos := [8][2]i32{{8, 10}, {12, 8}, {16, 6}, {24, 6}, {28, 8}, {32, 10}, {36, 12}, {34, 20}}\n\tfor hp in host_pos { topology_spawn_node(&s.topology, host_idx, hp, cat) }\n\tcamp_pos := [6][2]i32{{6, 20}, {10, 26}, {18, 28}, {26, 28}, {34, 26}, {36, 18}}\n\tfor cp in camp_pos { topology_spawn_node(&s.topology, camp_idx, cp, cat) }\n--- line 726:\n\ttesting.expectf(t, hosts >= 8, \"growth must place >= 8 streaming-capable terminals (content_hosts + campuses) by the surge window (got %d) — the aggregation crowd\", hosts)", "detail": "The re-pin seeds 8 hosts + 6 campuses directly, so `hosts >= 8` holds at spawn time and can never fail; the message still claims growth places them. The old growth-crowd guarantee silently stopped biting.", "recommended_fix": "Either reword to \"the seeded crowd survives\" or count only growth-spawned streaming terminals (node_slot >= seeded count) so the assertion bites again."}, {"source": "architecture", "severity": "note", "category": "claim-accuracy", "title": "PR body presents \"campus half lands fully\" as pinned, but W9 only asserts campus_window_spawns > 0", "location": "_bmad-output/pr-bodies/5.11.md:42 vs core/demand_test.odin:728", "evidence": "- **Campus half hard-pinned**: ≥1 campus must exist AND source in the window (a campus-silent pass is a regression), and the campus half lands fully (measured 100%).\n--- core/demand_test.odin:728 (the only campus-floor assertion in test_w9_surge_lands_under_caps):\n\ttesting.expectf(t, campus_window_spawns > 0, \"the honest surge floor requires a campus to SOURCE in the window (got %d in-window campus spawns)\", campus_window_spawns)", "detail": "\"Lands fully\" is a one-time measurement, not a pin; a regression where campuses land a small fraction passes while hosts + growth satisfy MIN_LAND. The 'hard-pinned' framing overstates the enforced floor.", "recommended_fix": "Pin the campus share explicitly (e.g. campus_window_spawns >= 10*WINDOW*95/100) or reword the claim to 'measured 100%, floored at >0'."}, {"source": "architecture", "severity": "note", "category": "consistency", "title": "Surge window derived from catalog in W9 but hardcoded 1200 in test_terminal_class_profiles", "location": "core/demand_test.odin:445 vs core/demand_test.odin:630-632", "evidence": "line 445 (test_terminal_class_profiles):\n\tSURGE_AT :: u64(1200) // the streaming surge's data start_tick\n--- lines 630-632 (test_w9_surge_lands_under_caps, same file):\n\tsurge := &cat.demand.eras[2].set_pieces[0]\n\tSURGE_START := u64(surge.start_tick)\n\tSURGE_END := SURGE_START + surge.duration_ticks", "detail": "W9's own comment says the window is derived \"so a future re-tune of the surge timing cannot silently drift this pin\", yet the sibling class-profiles test in the same file hardcodes 1200 — a surge re-tune would silently mislabel its base/surge split.", "recommended_fix": "Derive SURGE_AT from cat.demand.eras[2].set_pieces[0].start_tick in test_terminal_class_profiles as W9 does."}, {"source": "architecture", "severity": "note", "category": "memory-safety", "title": "run_inert discards record_run's [dynamic]u64 return — leaked hash buffer per call", "location": "core/demand_test.odin:546", "evidence": "\t\trun_inert :: proc(seed: u64, cat: ^Catalogs, ticks: u64) -> (by_class: [8]u64, src_hist: [8][64]u64, rng_state, rng_inc: u64) {\n\t\t\ts: Run_State\n\t\t\tdefer run_destroy(&s)\n\t\t\trun_init(&s, seed, cat.hash, TEST_LOGIC_HZ)\n\t\t\ts.era = 3\n\t\t\tqa_fixture(&s, cat) // residentials + router + content_host — no small_biz/campus\n\t\t\trecord_run(&s, ticks, cat)", "detail": "This is the suite's only record_run call site that drops the returned [dynamic]u64; each of the two calls leaks 600×8B — matches the paired `+++ leak 4.69KiB @ [determinism_test.odin:168:record_run()]` reports, violating the ODN-18 discipline the new test otherwise models.", "recommended_fix": "Capture and free: `hashes := record_run(&s, ticks, cat); defer delete(hashes)` inside run_inert."}]
